\title{9th Sunday after Pentecost 2026}
\tag{cmc}
\date{2026-07-26}
\author{liamoc}
\quote{
Deus in loco sancto suo: Deus, qui inhabitáre facit unánimes in domo: ipse dabit virtútem et fortitúdinem plebi suæ.
}
\p{I was once again the director of our choir at [All Saints Ainslie](https://allsaintsainslie.org.au), where we sang two anthems to a packed house: there were fourteen confirmees, and the bishop (and primate of Australia) came to
  induct them into the church. Our choir sang a favourite of mine, Lloyd's [View Me, Lord](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n4XdIWfdmlo), a lovely poem from Thomas Campion:}
\quote{
  \poem{
    \line{View me, Lord, a work of thine.}
    \line{Shall I then lie drown'd in night?}
    \line{Might thy grace in me but shine,}
    \line{I should seem made all of light.}
    \line{\br}
    \line{Cleanse me, Lord, that I may kneel}
    \line{At thine altar, pure and white.}
    \line{They that once thy mercies feel}
    \line{gaze no more on Earth's delight.}
    \line{\br}
    \line{Worldly joys, like shadows, fade}
    \line{When the heav'nly light appears;}
    \line{But the cov'nants thou hast made,}
    \line{Endless, know not days nor years.}
    \line{\br }
    \line{In thy word, Lord, is my trust;}
    \line{To thy mercies fast I fly.}
    \line{Though I am but clay and dust,}
    \line{Yet thy grace can lift me high.}
  }
}
\p{As well as Tallis' [If ye love me](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eqt005j1dB0), which, at least in my edition, was in the exact same key.}
\quote{
  \poem{
    \line{If ye love me, keep my commandments.}
    \line{And I will pray the Father,}
    \line{And He shall give you another comforter:}
    \line{That He may bide with you forever, e'en the Spirit of Truth.}
  }
}
\p{I also directed us for evensong, where we sang a mostly plainchant evensong, along with Stainer's [Hail, Gladdening Light](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hYmHdJJAyeA) as usual, plus Vaughan Williams' [The Call](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jg9QZ_Jeqqo) as an anthem (with solo verse sung by yours truly), from his settings
of George Herbert poems, the Five Mystical Songs.}
\quote{\poem{
\line{Come, my Way, my Truth, my Life;}
\line{Such a Way as gives us breath,}
\line{Such a Truth as ends all strife,}
\line{Such a Life as killeth death.}
\line{\br}
\line{Come, my Light, my Feast, my Strength;}
\line{Such a Light as shows a Feast,}
\line{Such a Feast as mends in length,}
\line{Such a Strength as makes his guest.}
\line{\br}
\line{Come, my Joy, my Love, my Heart;}
\line{Such a Joy as none can move,}
\line{Such a Love as none can part,}
\line{Such a Heart as joys in love.}
}}